title: Project Genesis: Ending the Hallucination Gap
type: manifesto
date: 2026-05-15
createdAt: 2026-05-15T07:00:00Z
releaseAt: 2026-05-15T15:00:00Z
author: Richard D.
stream: universal
tags: vision, manifesto, ikd-enablement

# The Founding Narrative
body[1]{content}:
  "Pharos began with a single realization: the commercial kitchen design industry is running on 'Opaque Truth.' For decades, Independent Kitchen Designers (IKDs) have been forced to hunt through bloated PDF catalogs and proprietary XML handlers, resulting in a 'Hallucination Gap' where the data in the model doesn't match the reality of the factory floor. Pharos exists to close that gap. By moving to a Metadata-First Standard driven by Rust and WASM, we are returning data sovereignty to the designer."

# Core Values
vision[3]{pillar, description}:
  Authoritative, "Data that is verified against the source of truth every 30 days."
  Deterministic, "Zero-host builds and memory-safe execution ensures consistency across platforms."
  Empowered, "IKDs gain high-leverage tools that automate the manual spec-hunting grind."

# The Standard
standard[1]{id, title, status}:
  v1.0, The Pharos Metadata Specification, Active
